|party=[[To be confirmed|TBC]]|region=England|county=[[Greater London]]|european=|elects_howmany=One}}'''Stratford and Bow''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume one: Report – London {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/2023-review-volume-one-report/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-one-report-london/ |access-date=2023-07-15 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it was first contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Stratford and Bow |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Stratford+and+Bow |access-date=2024-03-19 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>

==Constituency profile==
The population of Newham has grown significantly in the 21st century<ref>Office for National Statistics https://www.ons.gov.uk/visualisations/censusareachanges/E09000025</ref> so its representation increased from two seats to three in the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies|2023 boundary review]]. This seat includes [[Stratford, London|Stratford]] which has undergone extensive regeneration and hosted the [[2012 Olympic Games]]. [[Bow, London|Bow]] and [[Old Ford, London|Old Ford]] to the west and [[Forest Gate]] to the east have mostly Victorian housing with some post-war housing estates.

== Boundaries ==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Stratford and Bow (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}}
The constituency straddles the [[River Lea]] in [[East London]] and is composed of the following (as they existed on 1 December 2020):<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 3 London region}}</ref>
* The [[London Borough of Newham|Borough of Newham]] wards of [[Forest Gate]] North, Forest Gate South, [[Green Street, Newham|Green Street]] West, and [[Stratford, London|Stratford]] and New Town, transferred from [[West Ham (UK Parliament constituency)|West Ham]] (renamed [[West Ham and Beckton (UK Parliament constituency)|West Ham and Beckton]]).
* The [[London Borough of Tower Hamlets|Borough of Tower Hamlets]] wards of [[Bow, London|Bow]] East and Bow West, transferred from [[Bethnal Green and Bow (UK Parliament constituency)|Bethnal Green and Bow]] (renamed [[Bethnal Green and Stepney (UK Parliament constituency)|Bethnal Green and Stepney]])
* The Borough of Tower Hamlets ward of [[Bromley-by-Bow|Bromley]] North, transferred from [[Poplar and Limehouse (UK Parliament constituency)|Poplar and Limehouse]]
Following a local government boundary review in the Borough of Newham which came into effect in May 2022,<ref>{{Cite web |last=LGBCE |title=Newham {{!}} LGBCE |url=https://www.lgbce.org.uk/all-reviews/newham |access-date=2024-03-29 |website=www.lgbce.org.uk |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=The London Borough of Newham (Electoral Changes) Order 2021 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2021/613/contents/made}}</ref> the constituency now comprises the following from the 2024 general election:

* The London Borough of Newham wards of: Forest Gate North; Forest Gate South; Green Street West (nearly all); Maryland; Stratford; Stratford Olympic Park.
* The London Borough of Tower Hamlets wards of: Bow East; Bow West; Bromley North.<ref name=":1" />

