== Boundaries ==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Bromley and Biggin Hill (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|frame-width=150|frame-height=260|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}}
The constituency was defined as comprising the following wards of the [[London Borough of Bromley]] as they existed on 1 December 2020:

* Bickley; Biggin Hill; Bromley Common and Keston; Bromley Town; Darwin (part<sup>1</sup>); Hayes and Coney Hall; Plaistow and Sundridge.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 3 London region}}</ref>

<sup>1.</sup>Area marked “5” on the map of the Bromley and Biggin Hill constituency produced by the Boundary Commission for England<ref>{{Cite web |title=The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume three: Maps {{!}} Boundary Commission for England {{!}} Page 4 |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/2023-review-volume-three-maps/page/4/ |access-date=2023-12-28 |website=boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk |at=Map 118}}</ref>

It covers the following areas:<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bulbul |first=Nuray |date=2023-10-30 |title=What are the London constituencies for the next election? |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/news/london/london-constituencies-next-election-boundary-changes-b1116826.html |access-date=2023-12-28 |website=Evening Standard |language=en}}</ref>

* Just over half the electorate, comprising [[Bickley]], [[Bromley]], [[Plaistow, Bromley|Plaistow]] and [[Sundridge, London|Sundridge]], previously part of the abolished constituency of [[Bromley and Chislehurst (UK Parliament constituency)|Bromley and Chislehurst]]
* [[Bromley Common]], [[Keston]], [[Hayes, Bromley|Hayes]] and [[Coney Hall]], transferred from [[Beckenham (UK Parliament constituency)|Beckenham]] (renamed [[Beckenham and Penge (UK Parliament constituency)|Beckenham and Penge]])
* [[Biggin Hill]], transferred from [[Orpington (UK Parliament constituency)|Orpington]]
Following a local government boundary review which came into effect in May 2022,<ref>{{Cite web |last=LGBCE |title=Bromley {{!}} LGBCE |url=https://www.lgbce.org.uk/all-reviews/bromley |access-date=2024-03-28 |website=www.lgbce.org.uk |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=The London Borough of Bromley (Electoral Changes) Order 2021 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2021/424/contents/made}}</ref> the constituency now comprises the following wards of the London Borough of Bromley from the 2024 general election:

* Bickley and Sundridge; Biggin Hill; Bromley Common and Holwood; Bromley Town; Darwin (polling district DAR1); Hayes and Coney Hall; Plaistow; Shortlands and Park Langley (polling district SHP5X).<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Bromley and Biggin Hill |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Bromley+and+Biggin+Hill |access-date=2024-03-28 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>

