== Boundaries ==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Edmonton and Winchmore Hill (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}}
The constituency is composed of the following London Borough of Enfield wards: 

Bush Hill Park; Edmonton Green; Grange Park; Haselbury; Highfield; Jubilee; Lower Edmonton; Upper Edmonton; Winchmore Hill.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 3 London region}}</ref>

It comprises the following areas:<ref>{{Cite web |title=London: New Constituency Boundaries 2023 |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/bdy2023_lond_summary.html |access-date=2023-07-30 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>

* The majority of the abolished constituency of [[Edmonton (UK Parliament constituency)|Edmonton]], comprising the [[London Borough of Enfield|Borough of Enfield]] areas of [[Bush Hill Park]], [[Edmonton, London|Edmonton]] and Haselbury.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Edmonton and Winchmore Hill |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Edmonton%20and%20Winchmore%20Hill |access-date=2023-09-25 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>
* The [[London Borough of Enfield|Borough of Enfield]] areas of [[Grange Park, Enfield|Grange Park]], Highfield and [[Winchmore Hill]] from the abolished [[Enfield Southgate (UK Parliament constituency)|Enfield Southgate constituency]].<ref name=":0" />

