'''Kensington and Bayswater''' is a new [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]]. Proposed in [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]],<ref>{{Cite web |title=London {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/london/ |access-date=2023-06-20 |website=[[Boundary Commission for England]]}}</ref> which was made into law on 29 November 2023,<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |date=2023-11-29 |website=legislation.gov.uk |publisher=The National Archives |access-date=2024-03-29}}</ref> it will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].

The constituency name comes from the [[Central London]] areas of [[Kensington]] and [[Bayswater]].

== Boundaries ==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Kensington and Bayswater (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|frame-width=220|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}}
The constituency comprises the following wards: <ref>{{cite legislation UK|type=si|si=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023|year=2023|number=1230|accessdate=12 December 2023}}</ref>

* From the [[Royal Borough of Kensington and Chelsea]]: Abingdon, Brompton & Hans Town, Campden, Colville, Courtfield, Dalgarno, Earl's Court, Golborne, Holland, Norland, Notting Dale, Pembridge, Queen's Gate, St Helen's.
* From the [[City of Westminster]]: Bayswater, Lancaster Gate.

This means that it consists of nearly all the (former) constituency of [[Kensington (UK Parliament constituency)|Kensington]], two wards primarily from the abolished [[Westminster North (UK Parliament constituency)|Westminster North constituency]] and the southern half of the Brompton & Hans Town ward, which was transferred from the [[Chelsea and Fulham (UK Parliament constituency)|Chelsea and Fulham constituency]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Kensington and Bayswater |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Kensington%20and%20Bayswater |access-date=2023-09-25 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>

