{{Infobox UK constituency main|name=Queen's Park and Maida Vale|parliament=uk|image=[[File:Queen's Park and Maida Vale 2023 Constituency.svg|258px]]|caption=Boundary of Queen's Park and Maida Vale in [[Greater London]]|map_entity=Greater London|map_year=|year=[[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024]]|abolished=|type=Borough|previous=[[Westminster North (UK Parliament constituency)|Westminster North]], [[Brent Central (UK Parliament constituency)|Brent Central]] and [[Hampstead and Kilburn (UK Parliament constituency)|Hampstead and Kilburn]]|next=
|electorate= 75,256 (2023)<ref>{{cite web | url= https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-two-constituency-names-designations-and-composition/2023-volume-two-constituency-names-designations-and-composition-london/#lg_queens-park-and-maida-vale-bc-75256
|title= The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume two: Constituency names, designations and composition – London
 |publisher=Boundary Commission for England 
 |access-date=22 June 2024
 |df=dmy 
}}</ref>
|mp=[[To be confirmed|TBC]]
|party=[[To be confirmed|TBC]]|region=England|county=[[Greater London]]|european=|elects_howmany=One}}'''Queen's Park and Maida Vale''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]]. Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=London {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/london/ |access-date=2023-06-20 |website=[[Boundary Commission for England]]}}</ref>

== Boundaries ==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Queen's Park and Maida Vale (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}}
The constituency comprises the following areas:<ref>{{Cite web |title=London: New Constituency Boundaries 2023 |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/bdy2023_lond_summary.html |access-date=2023-07-30 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 3 London region}}</ref>

* The majority of the abolished constituency of [[Westminster North (UK Parliament constituency)|Westminster North]], comprising the [[City of Westminster]] wards of [[Church Street (ward)|Church Street]], Harrow Road, [[Little Venice (ward)|Little Venice]], [[Maida Vale (ward)|Maida Vale]], [[Queen's Park (Westminster ward)|Queen's Park]] and Westbourne.
* The [[London Borough of Brent|Borough of Brent]] wards of [[Harlesden]] and [[Kensal Green]], Kilburn, and [[Queens Park (Brent ward)|Queens Park]], transferred partly from [[Brent Central (UK Parliament constituency)|Brent Central]] (renamed [[Brent East (UK Parliament constituency)|Brent East]]) and [[Hampstead and Kilburn (UK Parliament constituency)|Hampstead and Kilburn]] (renamed [[Hampstead and Highgate (UK Parliament constituency)|Hampstead and Highgate]]).

