{{Short description|Parliamentary constituency in the United Kingdom, 2024 onwards}} {{Infobox UK constituency main|name=Southgate and Wood Green|parliament=uk|image=[[File:Southgate and Wood Green 2023 Constituency.svg|258px]]|caption=Boundary of Southgate and Wood Green in Greater London|map_entity=Greater London|map_year=|year=2024|abolished=|type=borough|previous=[[Enfield Southgate (UK Parliament constituency)|Enfield Southgate]], [[Hornsey and Wood Green (UK Parliament constituency)|Hornsey and Wood Green]] & [[Tottenham (UK Parliament constituency)|Tottenham]]|next= |electorate= 76,034 (2023)<ref>{{cite web | url= https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/the-2023-review-of-parliamentary-constituency-boundaries-in-england-volume-two-constituency-names-designations-and-composition/2023-volume-two-constituency-names-designations-and-composition-london/#lg_southgate-and-wood-green-bc-76034 |title= The 2023 Review of Parliamentary Constituency Boundaries in England – Volume two: Constituency names, designations and composition – London |publisher=Boundary Commission for England |access-date=22 June 2024 |df=dmy }}</ref> |mp=[[To be confirmed|TBC]] |party=[[To be confirmed|TBC]]|region=England|county=[[Greater London]]|european=|elects_howmany=One}}'''Southgate and Wood Green''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dispatch |first=Enfield |date=2023-06-30 |title=New 'Southgate and Wood Green' and 'Edmonton and Winchmore Hill' seats agreed |url=https://enfielddispatch.co.uk/new-southgate-and-wood-green-and-edmonton-and-winchmore-hill-seats-agreed/ |access-date=2023-09-25 |website=Enfield Dispatch |language=en-GB}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=London {{!}} Boundary Commission for England |url=https://boundarycommissionforengland.independent.gov.uk/2023-review/london/ |access-date=2023-06-20 |website=[[Boundary Commission for England]]}}</ref>
== Boundaries == {{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Southgate and Wood Green (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|frame-width=200|frame-height=260|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}} The constituency is composed of the following wards:
* The London Borough of Enfield wards of: Arnos Grove; Bowes; Cockfosters; New Southgate; Oakwood; Palmers Green; Southgate.
* The London Borough of Haringey wards of: Bounds Green; Noel Park; White Hart Lane; Woodside.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Parliamentary Constituencies Order 2023 |url=https://www.legislation.gov.uk/uksi/2023/1230/schedules/made |at=Schedule 1 Part 3 London region}}</ref>
It comprises the following areas:<ref>{{Cite web |title=London: New Constituency Boundaries 2023 |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/bdy2023_lond_summary.html |access-date=2023-07-30 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>
* The majority of the abolished constituency of [[Enfield Southgate (UK Parliament constituency)|Enfield Southgate]] in the [[London Borough of Enfield|Borough of Enfield]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Southgate and Wood Green |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Southgate%20and%20Wood%20Green |access-date=2023-09-25 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref> * Minority part ([[Wood Green]]) of the abolished constituency of [[Hornsey and Wood Green (UK Parliament constituency)|Hornsey and Wood Green]] in the [[London Borough of Haringey|Borough of Haringey]].<ref name=":0" /> * The [[White Hart Lane (ward)|White Hart Lane ward]] from the constituency of [[Tottenham (UK Parliament constituency)|Tottenham]] in the [[London Borough of Haringey|Borough of Haringey]].<ref name=":0" />
==Constituency profile== This is an ethnically diverse seat which showed strong support for Remain in the [[2016 United Kingdom European Union membership referendum|2016 EU referendum]]. Incomes and house prices are around average for Greater London.<ref>Electoral Calculus https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Southgate%20and%20Wood%20Green</ref>
